## Security Review: Critical Issues Found

### 🔴 Critical: SQL Injection
```javascript
// VULNERABLE - Direct string interpolation
const query = `SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${req.params.id}`;

// Attacker can pass: id = "1 OR 1=1"
// Resulting query: SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = 1 OR 1=1
// Returns ALL users in the database
```

### 🔴 Critical: No Authentication/Authorization
```javascript
// Anyone can query any user's data
// No check: "is the requester allowed to see this user?"
```

### 🔴 Critical: No Error Handling
```javascript
// Unhandled promise rejection exposes stack traces
// App can crash, leaking internal details to attackers
```

### 🟡 Serious: No Input Validation
```javascript
// No check that id is actually a number
// No length limits on the input
```

### 🟡 Serious: Over-fetching Data (`SELECT *`)
```javascript
// Returns ALL columns, potentially including
// passwords, tokens, SSNs, etc.
```

---

## ✅ Secured Version

```javascript
const { body, param, validationResult } = require('express-validator');

app.get('/api/users/:id',
  authenticate,                        // verify JWT/session
  param('id').isInt({ min: 1 }).trim(), // validate input
  async (req, res) => {
    // Check validation results
    const errors = validationResult(req);
    if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
      return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid user ID' });
    }

    // Authorization: users can only fetch their own data
    // (admins may be handled separately)
    if (req.user.id !== parseInt(req.params.id) && !req.user.isAdmin) {
      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
    }

    try {
      // Parameterized query prevents SQL injection
      const query = 'SELECT id, name, email, created_at FROM users WHERE id = ?';
      const user = await db.query(query, [req.params.id]);

      if (!user || user.length === 0) {
        return res.status(404).json({ error: 'User not found' });
      }

      res.json(user[0]);
    } catch (err) {
      // Log internally, don't expose details to client
      console.error('Database error:', err);
      res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
    }
  }
);
```

---

## Summary Table

| Issue | Severity | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| SQL Injection | 🔴 Critical | Parameterized queries |
| No auth/authz | 🔴 Critical | Middleware + ownership check |
| No error handling | 🔴 Critical | try/catch + generic errors |
| No input validation | 🟡 Serious | express-validator |
| SELECT * | 🟡 Serious | Explicit column names |

**The original code should never reach production.** SQL injection alone could expose or destroy your entire database.
